                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "35432af1-d108-442a-821a-17b755a500eb",
                                "sense_id": "7047b665-f878-3279-b545-a3b1bb36ae15",
                                "text": "There’s a word Trevor once told me about, one he learned from Buford, who served in the navy in Hawaii during the Korean War: kipuka. The piece of land that’s spared after a lava flow runs down the slope of a hill—an island formed from what survives the smallest apocalypse."
                            }
